'''''Weissia controversa''''', the '''green-tufted stubble-moss''',<ref Name=iucn/> is a species of moss in the [[Pottiaceae]] family.

It is widely found on all continents, except in [[Antarctica]].<ref name=iucn/> ''Weissia controversa'' is a [[hermaphrodite|hermaphroditic species]]. The plants usually grow to less than 1 cm in height and the spores measure 14–20 [[μm]].<ref>{{cite report |author=Jóhannsson, B. |language=is |date=1992 |title=Íslenskir mosar - Grýtumosaætt | trans-title=Icelandic Mosses - Pottiaceae |url=https://utgafa.ni.is/fjolrit/Fjolrit_21.pdf |publisher=Náttúrufræðistofnunu Íslands [Icelandic Institute of Natural History] |access-date=24 July 2021}}</ref>

